  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 88f6fa2b89436164b8e97b17d82dc9a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 3 - Inventory
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_inventory
  isUnlockedByDefault: 1
  ignoreLock: 0
  title: Inventory
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: '<b>Inventory</b>


    During exploration, you carry an Inventory
    that stores collected resources.


    The Inventory has a limited number of
    slots, and each resource occupies one slot regardless of type.


    Collected
    resources will fill empty slots in order from left to right.


    Each collected
    resource will display its value when obtained, allowing you to decide whether
    it is worth keeping or skipping.


    You can discard a stored resource using
    discard(i), where i is the slot index you want to remove. The index starts from
    0 up to inventory size - 1.


    There are separate Inventory capacities for
    Mineral Exploration and Material Exploration. Each can be upgraded independently
    to increase storage capacity.


    Manage your Inventory wisely, as space is
    limited during deeper expeditions.'
  isImageBig: 0
